<title>AUSTRALIA: NAB cuts fixed Australia housing loan rates.</title>
<headline>NAB cuts fixed Australia housing loan rates.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Australia Bank Ltd on Friday announced reductions in its fixed rate housing loan rates by up to a half of one percent.  </p>
<p>NAB said the new rates apply to owner-occuped and investor residential mortgages.</p>
<p>The new rates, effective from Monday, July 14, are:</p>
<p>				   New	Old    Change (pct)</p>
<p>    5 year		     7.75    7.99    -0.24</p>
<p>    4 year		     7.55    7.85    -0.30</p>
<p>    3 year		     7.25    7.60    -0.35</p>
<p>    2 year		     7.00    7.50    -0.50</p>
<p>    1 year		     6.70    7.10    -0.40</p>
<p>National Australia Bank chief general manager Frank Cicutto said rates had been cut following a downward trend in the wholesale market.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
